## How a route opts in

A router calls `.use(authPlugin)` or `.use(adminPlugin)` on its Elysia instance — typically right after creating it, protecting every route registered on that router:

**Regular session** — e.g. `packages/backend/src/api/access.ts`, `packages/backend/src/api/feedback.ts`, `packages/backend/src/api/crypto/reports.ts` (17 files total):
```ts
new Elysia({ prefix: "/api/..." })
    .use(authPlugin)
    .get(...)
```

**Admin session** — e.g. `packages/backend/src/api/admin/detection-patterns.ts` line 32, `admin/app-templates.ts` line 47 (all `/api/admin/*` routers):
```ts
new Elysia({ prefix: "/api/admin/..." })
    .use(adminPlugin)
    .get(...)
```

Routes that don't call `.use(authPlugin)` or `.use(adminPlugin)` are public — no session is required.

